# ============================================================================
# RescueNet AI — .gitignore
# Stack per docs/07-technology-selection.md: Python/FastAPI, PostgreSQL,
# Mosquitto, Kotlin/Android, React/Vite/TypeScript, Docker Compose.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS AND CREDENTIALS — never commit. Commit *.example templates instead.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.env
secrets/
secret/
credentials/
*credentials*
# Source code that *handles* credentials is not itself a credential. Verified
# 2026-08-24: the blanket rule above was silently untracking four real source
# files — `services/credentials.py`, `DeviceCredentialStore.kt`,
# `CredentialStoreTest.kt` and the Alembic migration `0003_m5_credentials.py` —
# so a fresh clone could neither build the app nor migrate the database.
# Credential *data* (.json/.env/.ini/.txt/…) stays ignored; only source is
# re-included.
!*credentials*.py
!*credentials*.kt
!*credentials*.kts
*secrets*
!*secrets*.example
*.secret
*.secrets

# API keys, tokens, device credentials (docs/09 Part 8)
*apikey*
*api_key*
*api-key*
*.token
tokens.json
device_tokens*
hmac_secret*
*.hmac

# MQTT — static password file and ACL hold credentials (docs/09 §4.4, AP-23)
deploy/mosquitto/passwd
deploy/mosquitto/passwd.*
deploy/mosquitto/pwfile*
deploy/mosquitto/acl
mosquitto_passwd*
!deploy/mosquitto/passwd.example
!deploy/mosquitto/acl.example
!deploy/mosquitto/mosquitto.conf

# SMS / carrier credentials (docs/09 Part 6)
sms_credentials*
*.sim
gateway_secret*

# Database credentials and connection strings
*.pgpass
.pgpass
pgpass*
database.ini
db_credentials*

# Certificates and private keys
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.csr
!**/*.pub

# Android signing material — a leaked keystore cannot be revoked
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore*
key.properties
signing.properties
release-signing*
google-services.json

